// Create Server in Node.js

To create a server in Node.js, we use the built-in http module.
const http = require("http");

const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {
    res.write("Hello from Node.js Server");
    res.end();
});

server.listen(3000, () => {
    console.log("Server running on port 3000");
});


// Explanation:
require("http") imports the core HTTP module
createServer() creates the server
req handles client requests
res sends response to the client
listen() starts the server on a port (3000)
Run the file and open http://localhost:3000
 in the browser 🚀